# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Steam credential and scratch files. Checked by check_gitignore.sh, which
#  upload.sh runs in every mode including a dry run.
#
#  This is the directory steamcmd is run from, so it is where its session state
#  lands. A committed session file is a handed-over build account: it authorises
#  uploading to the app without a password or a Steam Guard code, and revoking it
#  means rotating the account.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Everything generated: staged depot content, rendered VDFs, steamcmd's
# BuildOutput, upload logs, the synthetic fixture.
output/

# A local steamcmd install, if you keep one beside the scripts instead of on
# PATH. Contains config.vdf and the ssfn sentry files.
steamcmd/
sdk/

# ── Steam session state — never commit any of these ──────────────────────────
# config.vdf holds the cached, already-Steam-Guard-approved login token.
config.vdf
loginusers.vdf
# ssfn<digits> is the Steam Guard machine-authorisation ("sentry") file. Having
# one is what makes a machine "remembered", so it is equivalent to the second
# factor.
ssfn*
# Other names the sentry file has shipped under.
sentry
sentry.*
*.sentryfile
*.ssfn

# A local override of a build script (e.g. pointing ContentRoot at a scratch
# tree). Useful, never shared — the committed templates are the source of truth.
*.vdf.local
